
### 1. Create customer
POST http://localhost:8081/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Customer",
  "email": "orderitem-test-{{$timestamp}}@example.test",
  "phone": null
}

> {%
    client.test("Customer created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201");
    });
    if (response.status === 201 && response.body.id != null) {
        client.global.set("customerId", String(response.body.id));
    }
%}


### 2. Create order and save orderId
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "deliveryDate": "2026-11-01T12:00:00",
  "shippingAddressId": null,
  "status": "NEW"
}

> {%
    client.test("Order created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201");
    });
    if (response.status === 201 && response.body.id != null) {
        client.global.set("orderId", String(response.body.id));
    }
%}


### 3. Verify order exists
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json


### 4. POST orderitem
POST http://localhost:8081/orderitems
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "productId": 7,
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 19.90
}

> {%
    client.test("Item created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201");
    });
%}


### 5. GET created orderitem
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json


### 6. GET orderitems belonging to created order
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/items
Accept: application/json


### 7. PUT update orderitem
PUT http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5,
  "unitPrice": 17.50
}


### 8. Verify updated orderitem
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json


### 9. DELETE orderitem
DELETE http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}


### 10. Verify deletion - expected 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems/{{orderId}}/7
Accept: application/json


### 11. Verify order is empty
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/items
Accept: application/json


### 12. GET paginated orderitems
GET http://localhost:8081/orderitems?page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json


### 13. DELETE empty order
DELETE http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}


### 14. Verify order deletion - expected 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json
